method.description:
Replaces [member stream] with [param stream] and crossfades to it over [param duration] seconds: the playbacks of the current stream fade out from their gain and stop at the end, while [param stream] starts at gain [code]0.0[/code] and fades in. Emits [signal stream_changed] at once and [signal fade_finished] when the new stream has faded in. If the player is not playing, this sets the stream and calls [method fade_in].
The fading-out playbacks do not count for [member max_polyphony], do not emit [signal finished], and stop together with [method stop] or when the new stream ends first. [param stream] must not be [code]null[/code]; use [method fade_out] to fade to silence.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _on_level_started(level_music):
	$Music.crossfade_to(level_music, 2.0)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private void OnLevelStarted(AudioStream levelMusic)
{
	GetNode<AudioStreamPlayer>("Music").CrossfadeTo(levelMusic, 2.0f);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

signal.description:
Emitted when an [AudioStreamPlaylist] starts a track, also when the same track repeats (loop, shuffle). [param index] is the index in [member AudioStreamPlaylist.streams]. Not emitted for streams without tracks. The signal is emitted on the main thread, at most once per frame.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	$Music.track_changed.connect(func(index, stream): $NowPlaying.text = stream.resource_name)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
	GetNode<AudioStreamPlayer>("Music").TrackChanged += (index, stream) => GetNode<Label>("NowPlaying").Text = stream.ResourceName;
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
